  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nShower and storm coverage winds down early this morning now that\nthe cold front has completed its slow passage through the\nforecast area. One last batch of nocturnal convection was\nshifting southeastward at the time of writing, and should clip\nour southern zones within the next hours before a stretch of dry\nweather commences for the next several days.\n\nThe forecast area will relish within building high pressure\nbeginning today. Post-frontal northerly flow will also yield a\nbreak from this past week's heat wave, promoting Chamber of\nCommerce weather conditions for the rest of the Labor Day\nholiday weekend. This will feature cooler temperatures, lowered\nhumidity, and mostly clear skies.\n\nTemperatures will then steadily climb back above their\nclimatological norms heading into midweek as the orientation of\nthe surface high shifts east. The return of onshore flow and\nrising upper level heights will then encourage daytime highs to\nbranch back into the lower 90s for parts of the Tri-State area,\nbut remaining dry through the day Wednesday.\n\nA cold front approaches late Wednesday night, yielding the\nreturn of showers and storms for the second half of the work\nweek.",
